# The proposal

A proposal is one JSON object, given as `proposal` to `autopilot_check` and `autopilot_propose`. The user reviews it in the Autopilot tab as one card, whose parts apply in this order: `prompts`, then `routines`, then `settings`, then `rules`, so a routine may run a prompt the same proposal adds. The user applies or discards each part on its own.

```
Proposal {
  summary: string
  prompts?: NewPrompt[]
  routines?: RoutineChange[]
  settings?: SettingsChange
  rules?: RulesChange
}
NewPrompt {
  name: string
  nickname: string
  purpose: "agent" | "reply"
  replyAction?: "approve" | "request_changes" | "comment"
  appliesTo: "pr" | "issue" | "any"
  body: string
}
RoutineChange {
  id?: number
  base?: string
  name: string
  description?: string
  mode?: "dryRun" | "ask" | "auto"
  template?: string
  spec: Spec  // a routine's definition: topic routine
}
SettingsChange {
  defaultMode?: "dryRun" | "ask" | "auto"
  agentsAtOnce?: number
  runsPerDay?: number
  actionsPerDay?: number
  actionsPerHour?: number
  dailyCap?: DailyCap
  keepAwake?: boolean
  holdOnOutage?: boolean
  catchUpHours?: number
  historyDays?: number
  logDays?: number
}
RulesChange {
  trust?: string[]
  untrust?: string[]
  pin?: string[]
  mute?: string[]
  clear?: string[]
  ignoreWorkflows?: string[]
  unignoreWorkflows?: string[]
}
DailyCap {
  amount: number
  unit: "usd" | "tokens"
}
```

- `summary`: one or two sentences, in plain words, that the card shows first: what the proposal does.
- `prompts`: new prompts for the library (topic `prompts`).
- `routines`: new routines, and changes to the user's routines. `name` is one line of at most 80 characters, and `description` at most 500; a name another routine has takes a free one, as a save would. `spec` is its whole definition (topic `routine`), and `template` the gallery template it starts from, if any (topic `templates`).
- A new routine has no `id`. Its `mode` is the mode you suggest: the card shows it as a hint beside the mode the routine starts in, which Settings gives new routines, and never applies it.
- A change to one of the user's routines gives its `id`, and its `updatedAt` from `autopilot_my_setup` as `base`, exactly as written there, so the card can say if it changed since you read it. It gives the routine's `name` (its own, unless the user asks for another), its `description`, and its whole `spec` as it should be once changed. It has no `mode`: a routine keeps its own mode and switch.
- `settings`: only the settings that change (topic `settings`).
- `rules`: the rules to change (topic `rules`).

A proposal holds at most 10 routines and 10 prompts, and one that holds nothing is refused. Every key is spelled exactly as above: a key the format doesn't have, or one spelled in another case, is refused, and so is a key given twice.

## A worked example

This example holds every part at once to show the format; a real proposal holds only what the user asked for. It starts from a template, runs a new prompt in place of the template's, caps Autopilot's daily spend, and mutes a repository.

```json
{
  "summary": "Fixes failing checks on your pull requests in the background with a new prompt that starts with the tests, caps Autopilot at $5 a day, and mutes acme-org/legacy.",
  "prompts": [
    {
      "name": "Fix failing checks, starting with the tests",
      "nickname": "Tests first",
      "purpose": "agent",
      "appliesTo": "pr",
      "body": "Fix the failing checks on {{.Repo}} #{{.Number}} ({{.FailedChecks}}). Start with the tests: run them, read what fails, fix the cause, and push once."
    }
  ],
  "routines": [
    {
      "name": "Fix failing checks on my PRs",
      "description": "Fixes the failing checks on my pull requests, starting with the tests.",
      "mode": "ask",
      "template": "fix-failing-checks-on-my-prs",
      "spec": {
        "version": 1,
        "watch": {
          "sources": [
            {
              "lists": [
                "authored"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "trigger": {
          "event": "checks_failed",
          "waitForChecks": true
        },
        "conditions": {
          "match": "all",
          "of": [
            {
              "field": "pr.draft",
              "op": "isNo"
            }
          ]
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "agent": {
              "agent": "inherit",
              "prompt": {
                "nickname": "Tests first"
              },
              "where": "background",
              "fence": {
                "tools": "editTestPush"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "waitForChecks": {},
            "onlyIf": "pushed"
          },
          {
            "tellMe": {
              "when": "verdict"
            }
          }
        ],
        "limits": {
          "oncePer": "headCommit",
          "triesPerItem": 2
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "settings": {
    "dailyCap": {
      "amount": 5,
      "unit": "usd"
    }
  },
  "rules": {
    "mute": [
      "acme-org/legacy"
    ]
  }
}
```
